# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: usb0 identifies and runs its controller as usb-test's
# does, enumerates QEMU's USB audio device on root port 5, starts its
# isochronous OUT endpoint with a 440 Hz tone and reports its first 10 s with
# no interval missed. With QEMU_SETTLE=600 the test runs ten minutes more,
# and a missed interval at any time fails it.
NOWAYOS: usb0: starting
NOWAYOS: usb0: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb0: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb0: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb0: ready
NOWAYOS: usb0: port 5: device 46f4:0002, class 0/0/0, USB 1.0, full-speed
NOWAYOS: usb0: port 5: endpoint 0x01 out: interface 1, alternate 1: 48000 Hz, 2 channels of 16 bits, up to 192 bytes every 1000 us, 48 transfers ahead: a 440 Hz tone
NOWAYOS: usb0: port 5: endpoint 0x01 out: 10 s, no interval missed

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# a PD giving up, an event refused, a device left alone, a stream not
# streamed, or an interval missed.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!refused
!left alone
!not streamed
!missed so far
